# DTF tier manifest: oci-conformance
# =============================================================================
# Adopts the upstream OCI distribution-spec conformance suite
# (github.com/opencontainers/distribution-spec, conformance/) and points it at
# Artifact Keeper's /v2 registry. This is the ONE ecosystem with a purpose-built
# "point at any server" conformance suite; running it unmodified is the highest-
# ROI brick of the conformance-corpus program (see docs/test-framework-2026.md).
#
# Topology: filesystem / single. The suite runs inside a golang container on the
# host network (--network host) so it reaches AK at the slot's published
# 127.0.0.1:${HTTP_PORT}. NEEDS_INTERNET: the container clones the pinned
# distribution-spec ref and downloads its Go module deps on first run.
#
# The oracle:
#   * creates two hosted OCI repos (OCI_NAMESPACE / OCI_CROSSMOUNT_NAMESPACE),
#   * runs the suite with PULL + PUSH + CONTENT_DISCOVERY enabled (the workflows
#     AK is expected to pass),
#   * ingests the suite's junit.xml into results/ and asserts zero
#     failures/errors across those workflows,
#   * leaves CONTENT_MANAGEMENT (delete) OFF by default (OCI_CONFORMANCE_DELETE=1
#     to enable) because AK's blob-delete path is a known conformance gap
#     (DELETE /v2/<name>/blobs/<digest> currently 405s) — enabling it is how we
#     track closing that gap rather than a silent skip.
#
# Pin: OCI_CONFORMANCE_REF (default a tagged distribution-spec release) keeps the
# env-var contract and suite behavior deterministic across runs.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the suite drives many back-to-back blob/manifest
# pushes and pulls through a single admin principal.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
NEEDS_INTERNET="true"
